(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[17 1 "// The AOT's side of the runtime (PY8; doc/python/PYTHON-SURVEY.md §7, PYS13 (a); doc/python/PYI-SPEC.md"] [18 1 "// §10): arbace.python.aot translates each code object's IR into a Go function over this package, a"] [19 1 "// compiled interpreter: the instructions become Go statements calling the helpers below with their"] [20 1 "// arguments as constants, the jumps gotos, the decoding and the dispatch loop's switch gone. The"] [21 1 "// frame stays the machine's heap frame (its stack, locals, cells, PC and Lasti), so a compiled"] [22 1 "// function is run by the same loop (Thread.run) in place of step: a call of a Python function still"] [23 1 "// pushes the callee's frame (the Go stack never holds Python frames, RecursionError where CPython"] [24 1 "// raises it), an exception unwinds by the code's exception table, and a generator's or coroutine's"] [25 1 "// frame is resumed by the function's entry switch on its PC (a state machine over the heap frame)."] [26 1 "//"] [27 1 "// A compiled program registers its modules' IR (the loader's text) with their native functions in"] [28 1 "// pre-order (the code object, then its nested code objects in constant order); the loader attaches"] [29 1 "// them (ReadIR's irLoadedHook). Source compiled at run time (exec, eval, compile, an import of a module"] [30 1 "// not compiled ahead) goes to the host's compiler (PYI_AOT_COMPILER, arbace.python.aot compile-server)"] [31 1 "// and runs on the dispatch loop."] [34 41 "// AotKey(mode, source) -> the IR text compiled ahead"] [35 41 "// the IR text -> its code objects' native functions"] [39 1 "// aotLoop (PYI_AOT_LOOP set) leaves every code object to the loop: the compiled program run as pyi runs it,"] [40 1 "// the check's interpreted reference on the same runtime and its speed's baseline."] [45 1 "// AotKey is the key of a source text compiled ahead in mode (exec, eval, single): its SHA-256 in hex."] [51 1 "// AotRegister registers a module compiled ahead: key its source's (AotKey; \"\" for the main module,"] [52 1 "// which AotMain runs from its text), ir its IR text, natives its code objects' functions in pre-order."] [60 1 "// aotAttach is ReadIR's hook: the native functions of a registered IR text set on its code objects."] [87 1 "// aotCompile is a compiled program's compiler (SetCompiler): a source compiled ahead, else the host's IR cache's"] [88 1 "// answer, else the host's."] [99 1 "// The host's IR cache (202b): the host's compiler (arbace.python.run/compile-source) keeps each answer it can keep in"] [100 1 "// WORK/ir-cache/KK/KEY, KEY the SHA-256 of \"MODE\\x00DIGEST\\x00SOURCE\", DIGEST its compiler's (the SHA-256 of its"] [101 1 "// sources). The compiler's script (PYI_AOT_COMPILER, bin/pyi's aot_module) names them on a line \"# ir-cache: DIR"] [102 1 "// DIGEST\"; a compiled program reads that cache itself, the answer the host would read first, so a run whose sources"] [103 1 "// at run time were all compiled before starts no host (about 0.6 s of every compiled program's start on the VM)."] [146 1 "// hostCompile asks the host's compiler (the command PYI_AOT_COMPILER names, started once: arbace.python.aot"] [147 1 "// compile-server) for source's IR: a request \"MODE\\tFILE\\tBYTES\\n\" and the source, an answer \"BYTES\\n\""] [148 1 "// and the compiler's text (arbace.python.run/compile-source's: the IR, SyntaxError: ..., incomplete)."] [199 1 "// AotMain is a compiled program's process: sys.argv and sys.path as bin/pyi run gives them, the"] [200 1 "// compiler of source at run time, the main module's IR run as __main__ (RunModule); the exit status."] [201 1 "// PYI_AOT_STATS names a file for the code objects run compiled and on the loop, and the host's compiles."] [205 2 "// Go's collector (202b): a compiled program allocates fast and keeps little (its live heap tens of MB), so"] [206 2 "// GOGC's default of 100 collects every few tens of MB, 20-30% of a benchmark's time on the VM; 400 unless"] [207 2 "// GOGC says otherwise, under a soft limit of 2 GiB unless GOMEMLIMIT says otherwise (past it Go collects as"] [208 2 "// often as it must)"] [233 1 "// AotBadPC is a compiled function entered at a PC that is not an instruction's."] [238 1 "// The helpers of the compiled code: each is an operation of step's switch (eval.go) with its argument"] [239 1 "// a constant; the ones that may raise return the error, a call also a *pushFrame."] [437 1 "// AotToBool is to-bool (not false) and not (not true)."] [530 1 "// AotLoadAttr is load-attr of name i at instruction pc (its inline cache's, attr.go's loadAttrAt; 202b: it went"] [531 1 "// through AotExec and the registered operation)."] [541 1 "// AotLoadMethod is load-attr of name i at instruction pc when a call of the attribute with N simple arguments"] [542 1 "// follows (arbace.python.aot's method calls; queue 210, CPython's LOAD_ATTR's method variant): a Python function"] [543 1 "// found on an instance's type and not in its dict pushed with the instance after it (no bound method made), any"] [544 1 "// other attribute pushed with noSelf after it; AotCallMethod calls either."] [566 3 "// a built-in container's method (no instance dict): the method descriptor with the object, as descrGet"] [567 3 "// binds it"] [590 1 "// noSelf (&noSelf) is AotLoadMethod's mark of an attribute that is not a method to call with its instance: a"] [591 1 "// variable without an initializer (no init-order entry), not zero-sized, so its address is its own."] [598 1 "// AotCallMethod is call [N] after AotLoadMethod: the function with the instance first, else the attribute called."] [607 22 "// CALL, C_RETURN, C_RAISE (queue 220): the method and self, its first argument"] [641 1 "// AotStoreAttr is store-attr of name i at instruction pc."] [692 1 "// AotForIter is for-iter: the next item pushed (false), or at the end the iterator popped (true)."] [697 22 "// FOR_ITER clears a raised StopIteration: the loop's end"] [710 1 "// AotTruthy is the popped value's truth (the conditional jumps')."] [744 1 "// AotCall is call [N KWNAMES] (kw the kwnames tuple's constant index, or -1): a Python function's"] [745 1 "// frame pushed (the *pushFrame returned: f.PC must be the next instruction's), a generator made, or"] [746 1 "// any other callable called."] [750 22 "// CALL, C_RETURN, C_RAISE (queue 220)"] [788 31 "// as OpMakeFunction (queue 205f)"] [806 1 "// AotExec runs instruction i of f's code as step runs it, for the operations the compiled code does not"] [807 1 "// spell out: the rarer ones of step's switch and every operation another file registers (RegisterOp)."] [808 1 "// f.PC is the next instruction's when it is called; an operation that jumps sets it."] [940 1 "// AotPopIsNone pops the top and tells whether it is None (jump-if-none, jump-if-not-none)."] [943 1 "// The register generator's helpers (queue 216): arbace.python.aot keeps the value stack in the compiled function's Go"] [944 1 "// locals within a basic block, so these take their operands as arguments and return their results; the frame's stack"] [945 1 "// holds only what was written back (doc/python/PYTHON-SURVEY.md, \"Design: 216\")."] [947 1 "// AotDrop truncates f's stack to n items (the compiled code took the rest into its locals, or popped them)."] [953 1 "// AotSpill writes the compiled code's locals back onto f's stack, in stack order."] [961 1 "// AotStackCall is AotCallV's and AotCallMethodV's answer that the call goes the stack's way, nothing of it done yet:"] [962 1 "// the compiled code writes its locals back and calls AotCall or AotCallMethod (a Python function not compiled, whose"] [963 1 "// frame runFrames pushes, or directMax direct calls already nested; queue 216d)."] [970 1 "// AotCallV is call [N KWNAMES] (kw the kwnames tuple's constant index, or -1) with the callable and its N arguments,"] [971 1 "// xs, the compiled code's locals, callStack's cases in callStack's order (queue 216d): a compiled Python function's"] [972 1 "// frame (a bound method's, self first in the callable's place; a class's __init__ callInit runs, the instance in it)"] [973 1 "// run directly by runDirect and its value returned, a generator made, any other callable called; AotStackCall for a"] [974 1 "// frame runFrames must push. xs is the call's own (Go's variadic array, never kept: copied where a callee may keep it)."] [978 49 "// CALL, C_RETURN, C_RAISE (queue 220; a stack call's are callStack's)"] [1025 1 "// AotCallMethodV is call [N] after AotLoadMethodV, xs its two values (the function, builtin or attribute, then self or"] [1026 1 "// noSelf) and the N arguments, the compiled code's locals: AotCallMethod's cases, a compiled function run directly;"] [1027 1 "// AotStackCall as AotCallV's."] [1033 46 "// CALL, C_RETURN, C_RAISE (queue 220): the method and self, its first argument"] [1048 1 "// aotStacked is whether AotCallV or AotCallMethodV returns AotStackCall for callable (its events then callStack's)."] [1057 1 "// stackCall is a call of fn from compiled code the stack's way (AotStackCall): its code not compiled, or directMax direct"] [1058 1 "// calls nested; a generator's or coroutine's function never (the call only makes its object)."] [1064 1 "// callFunctionV is a call of the Python function fn with args from compiled code: its generator made, or its compiled"] [1065 1 "// frame run directly; AotStackCall, nothing done, when it goes the stack's way."] [1140 1 "// AotLoadGlobalV is load-global of name i at instruction pc (its cache's index a constant)."] [1154 1 "// AotTruthy2 is a value's truth, the bools answered without a call."] [1204 1 "// AotLoadAttrV is load-attr of name i at instruction pc."] [1209 1 "// AotLoadMethodV is AotLoadMethod with its operand an argument: the callable and the instance (or noSelf)."] [1245 1 "// AotStoreAttrV is store-attr of name i at instruction pc: o.name = v."] [1252 1 "// AotNext is for-iter's next item, nil at the end (a raised Sto